 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a completed preview is admitted to the cache, the system SHALL admit it to the short-term queue (the first-use queue of the 2Q replacement policy).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When the short-term queue is at its configured share of the 12 GiB budget, the system SHALL evict its oldest preview to admit a new one, without evicting any main-queue preview.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a preview held in the short-term queue is requested again, the system SHALL move it to the main queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When the main queue is at its configured share of the 12 GiB budget, the system SHALL evict its least-recently-used preview before moving a short-term preview into it.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When a preview held in the main queue is requested again, the system SHALL record it as most recently used.
